pr_comments:
@jaypatrickhoward The current behavior is to use raw mode when output is not a TTY (e.g. piping to a script), and use "standard" mode (which is really quoted) for interactive sessions.

Another addition is `--quoted-input` which forces de-quoting of inputs, which until now was only done when input was a TTY (in an interactive session).

@miluChen the PR was incomplete, you should now be able to do that using `--quoted-input --prefix`.

